<title>HONG KONG: Sui Chong 1996 net profit falls sharply.</title>
<headline>Sui Chong 1996 net profit falls sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.33	 vs  7.20</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs  6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  16.87 loss vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    2.89	 vs  13.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		     394.81     vs  156.17</p>
<p>    Company name		 Sui Chong Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Construction and property concern Sui Chong, a subsidiary of Winfoong Investment Ltd, is the successor company of the MKI Corp after a rescue plan.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss of HK$16.87 million representing the excess of revaluation deficit of investment properties over the revaluation surplus in the investment property revaluation reserve.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
